// Back: a clean stroked chevron.
//
// This replaces a "dotted chevron" built from 2.86-unit blocks. That staircase
// was the point of the old glyph, but 2.86 is not a whole number of pixels at
// any common scale, so every block edge landed mid-pixel and the arrow read as
// low-resolution rather than as deliberate pixel art.
//
// TWO CANVAS REPS. Chromium picks the rep matching the requested size, so the
// 16 rep is drawn at 16 rather than scaled down from 24 -- which is what
// actually makes it crisp in the toolbar. Coordinates in each rep are whole or
// half units so the stroke sits on the pixel grid.
//
// FLIPS_IN_RTL: a back arrow points the other way in right-to-left locales,
// and the old glyph never did.

CANVAS_DIMENSIONS, 24,
FLIPS_IN_RTL,
STROKE, 2.f,
CAP_SQUARE,
MOVE_TO, 15, 5,
LINE_TO, 8, 12,
LINE_TO, 15, 19,
CLOSE

CANVAS_DIMENSIONS, 16,
FLIPS_IN_RTL,
STROKE, 1.5f,
CAP_SQUARE,
MOVE_TO, 10, 3.5f,
LINE_TO, 5.5f, 8,
LINE_TO, 10, 12.5f,
CLOSE
